\section{Stat, Prob, and Mean}{

Every \verb{PM_*} function returns a \link[=pm-class]{pm} object with three related
summaries: \code{Stat} is the raw metric above, computed per simulation (and
averaged over the evaluation window for the Yield-family metrics); \code{Prob}
is the per-simulation probability/indicator of meeting the stated
objective (\code{NA} for metrics with no such objective, e.g. \code{PM_Yield});
\code{Mean} is \code{Prob} averaged across simulations, or — for metrics with no
\code{Prob} — \code{Stat} averaged across simulations instead.
}

